    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe owner response DTO (`OwnerDto`) is generated from the OpenAPI spec, so I wired the feature through the spec, the entity, and the mapper:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `displayName` field.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient` computed getter:\n   ```java\n   @Transient\n   public String getDisplayName() {\n       return this.getLastName() + \", \" + this.getFirstName();\n   }\n   ```\n   `@Transient` keeps JPA from treating it as a persisted column.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 MapStruct now auto-maps `displayName` (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`: `ownerDto.setDisplayName(owner.getDisplayName())`), since both the entity getter and DTO setter exist. No manual mapping code needed.\n\n4. **Test** \u2014 Added `createOwnerReturnsDisplayName` asserting a created George Franklin returns `$.displayName == \"Franklin, George\"`.\n\n## Results\n- Full suite: **268 \u2192 all pass** (added 1 new test \u2192 269 total, owner controller now 25 tests, all green).\n- The `displayName` is computed on owner creation and returned in the response formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`.",
